  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10460v2</id>
    <title>Cycling along Euler road</title>
    <updated>2025-11-06T14:19:55Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.10460v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.10460v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We introduce the notion of $P_λ$ points, which canonically parametrize points on the Euler line. This allows us to show that the Euler line of any $d$-dimensional inscribed polygon in Euclidean space arises from the Euler lines of its sub-polygons, beginning from the Euler line of a point in the plane. Furthermore, we situate $P_λ$ points in the literature of modern triangle centers.</summary>
    <category term="math.MG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.HO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
